::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q01
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 6 + 2 times 5.
{
=A. 16#Correct. Multiply first: 2 times 5 = 10. Then 6 + 10 = 16.
~B. 40#This adds 6 + 2 first, then multiplies. Multiplication comes before addition here.
~C. 13#This does not correctly apply multiplication before addition. Start with 2 times 5.
~D. 30#This multiplies 6 times 5 and ignores the structure of the expression.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q02::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q02
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate (9 - 3)^2.
{
~A. 12#This subtracts but does not square the result. The exponent still applies.
~B. 78#This squares 9 and subtracts 3. Grouping symbols must be simplified first.
=C. 36#Correct. First 9 - 3 = 6. Then 6^2 = 36.
~D. 6#This stops after evaluating inside the parentheses. The exponent must still be evaluated.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q03::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q03
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 20 - 4 times 3.
{
~A. 48#This subtracts first, then multiplies. Multiplication must be completed before subtraction.
=B. 8#Correct. First 4 times 3 = 12. Then 20 - 12 = 8.
~C. 17#This subtracts 3 from 20 and does not use 4 times 3 correctly.
~D. 12#This stops after multiplication and does not complete the subtraction.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q04::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q04
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 5^2 + 6.
{
~A. 11#This adds 5 and 6 without evaluating the exponent. Exponents come before addition.
~B. 55#This may treat the exponent as multiplication by 2 after adding. Evaluate 5^2 first.
~C. 36#This squares 6 instead of 5. The exponent applies only to 5.
=D. 31#Correct. 5^2 = 25, and 25 + 6 = 31.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q05::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q05
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 24 / 6 + 7.
{
=A. 11#Correct. Divide first: 24 / 6 = 4. Then 4 + 7 = 11.
~B. 2#This adds 6 + 7 first, then divides. Addition does not come before division here.
~C. 4#This stops after the division and does not add 7.
~D. 17#This may divide incorrectly or add before simplifying. Complete 24 / 6 first.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q06::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q06
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 3(4 + 5).
{
~A. 17#This adds 3 + 4 + 5 instead of multiplying by the grouped value.
=B. 27#Correct. First 4 + 5 = 9. Then 3 times 9 = 27.
~C. 23#This multiplies 3 times 4 and then adds 5. The grouping symbols must be simplified first.
~D. 12#This multiplies 3 times 4 and ignores the + 5 inside the parentheses.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q07::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q07
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 18 / 3 times 2.
{
~A. 3#This multiplies 3 times 2 first. Multiplication and division are completed from left to right.
~B. 6#This stops after 18 / 3. The expression also includes times 2.
~C. 36#This multiplies 18 times 2 and ignores the division order.
=D. 12#Correct. Work from left to right: 18 / 3 = 6, then 6 times 2 = 12.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q08::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q08
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 14 - 6 + 2.
{
~A. 6#This subtracts the sum 6 + 2 from 14. Addition and subtraction are completed from left to right.
~B. 22#This adds all the numbers and ignores the subtraction sign.
~C. 12#This adds 6 + 2 after subtracting incorrectly. Work from left to right.
=D. 10#Correct. Work left to right: 14 - 6 = 8, and 8 + 2 = 10.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q09::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q09
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 2^3 + 4 times 2.
{
=A. 16#Correct. 2^3 = 8 and 4 times 2 = 8, so 8 + 8 = 16.
~B. 20#This may add 8 + 4 first, then multiply. Multiplication must be completed before addition.
~C. 14#This treats 2^3 as 6. Remember that 2^3 means 2 times 2 times 2.
~D. 24#This multiplies after adding terms. Follow exponent and multiplication before addition.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q10::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q10
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate (8 + 2) / 5.
{
~A. 9.6#This divides 2 by 5 first. Grouping symbols must be simplified first.
~B. 10#This stops after simplifying the grouping symbols. The division must still be completed.
~C. 15#This adds 8 + 2 + 5 instead of dividing by 5.
=D. 2#Correct. First 8 + 2 = 10. Then 10 / 5 = 2.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q11::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q11
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 4x + 1 when x = 3.
{
~A. 8#This adds 4 + 3 + 1 instead of multiplying 4 by the value of x.
=B. 13#Correct. Substitute 3 for x: 4(3) + 1 = 12 + 1 = 13.
~C. 12#This stops after 4 times 3 and does not add 1.
~D. 16#This adds 4 to the product instead of adding 1. Check the expression carefully.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q12::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q12
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 6n - 2 when n = 5.
{
~A. 24#This may subtract before multiplying. Substitute first, then multiply before subtracting.
~B. 30#This stops after 6 times 5 and does not subtract 2.
=C. 28#Correct. Substitute 5 for n: 6(5) - 2 = 30 - 2 = 28.
~D. 33#This adds instead of subtracting after substitution.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q13::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q13
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate a^2 + 3 when a = 4.
{
=A. 19#Correct. Substitute 4 for a: 4^2 + 3 = 16 + 3 = 19.
~B. 11#This doubles 4 instead of squaring 4. The exponent means 4 times 4.
~C. 25#This adds first and then squares. There are no grouping symbols around a + 3.
~D. 16#This stops after evaluating the exponent and does not add 3.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q14::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q14
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 2(y + 6) when y = 3.
{
~A. 12#This multiplies 2 times 6 and ignores the value substituted for y.
~B. 15#This adds 2 + 3 + 6 instead of multiplying by the grouped value.
=C. 18#Correct. Substitute 3 for y: 2(3 + 6) = 2(9) = 18.
~D. 36#This multiplies 2 times 3 times 6 instead of simplifying inside the grouping symbols.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q15::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q15
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 5m / 2 when m = 6.
{
~A. 13#This adds 5 + 6 + 2 instead of using multiplication and division.
~B. 60#This multiplies all three numbers. The expression says to divide by 2 after multiplying.
~C. 30#This stops after 5 times 6 and does not divide by 2.
=D. 15#Correct. Substitute 6 for m: 5(6) / 2 = 30 / 2 = 15.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q16::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q16
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 3p + 2^2 when p = 4.
{
~A. 20#This may add 3(4) and 2, but 2 must be squared.
=B. 16#Correct. Substitute 4 for p: 3(4) + 2^2 = 12 + 4 = 16.
~C. 24#This treats 2^2 as a multiplier or combines steps incorrectly.
~D. 14#This adds only 2 instead of evaluating 2^2.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q17::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q17
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 30 - (4 + 2)^2.
{
=A. -6#Correct. First 4 + 2 = 6. Then 6^2 = 36. Finally 30 - 36 = -6.
~B. 24#This subtracts 6 from 30 and does not square the grouped value.
~C. 28#This squares only 2 or does not apply the grouping symbols correctly.
~D. 34#This adds instead of subtracting after evaluating the grouped expression.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q18::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q18
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 7 + 18 / 3.
{
~A. 25#This adds 7 + 18 first. Division must be completed before addition.
=B. 13#Correct. Divide first: 18 / 3 = 6. Then 7 + 6 = 13.
~C. 8.3#This appears to divide after adding. Follow the order of operations.
~D. 6#This stops after the division and does not add 7.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q19::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q19
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 4(10 - 7) + 5.
{
~A. 7#This simplifies only 10 - 7 and adds 4 incorrectly. The 4 means multiplication.
~B. 12#This adds 10 - 7 + 5 and ignores multiplication by 4.
=C. 17#Correct. First 10 - 7 = 3. Then 4(3) + 5 = 12 + 5 = 17.
~D. 32#This multiplies 4 times 10 - 7 incorrectly. Grouping symbols must be simplified first.
}

::ALG1_U01_L04_Quiz_Q20::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L04_Q20
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate 100 / (2^2 + 6).
{
~A. 56#This divides 100 by 2 first or combines operations out of order. Start inside the grouping symbols.
~B. 25#This uses only 2^2 in the denominator and ignores + 6.
=C. 10#Correct. Inside the parentheses, 2^2 + 6 = 4 + 6 = 10. Then 100 / 10 = 10.
~D. 96#This subtracts the denominator from 100 instead of dividing.
}

